cosmic-session spawns cosmic-settings-daemon and, without waiting for it
to actually come up on the session bus, immediately goes on to start
cosmic-osd and the rest of the session components. Every COSMIC app
(via libcosmic's cosmic-config crate) watches a handful of configs
(com.system76.CosmicTk, com.system76.CosmicTheme.Mode,
com.system76.CosmicTheme.Dark, ...) by asking cosmic-settings-daemon
over D-Bus to set up the watch. Because process_manager.start() only
waits for the process to spawn -- not for it to register its
"com.system76.CosmicSettingsDaemon" bus name -- cosmic-osd's first
watch_config/watch_state calls can hit the bus before the daemon is
actually there, which logs a "Failed to create watcher for ..." error
(cosmic-config retries with exponential backoff and succeeds a moment
later, but the spurious error is printed on every boot). Wait for the
daemon's D-Bus name to actually be owned before starting the components
that depend on it, closing the race at the source instead of relying on
the retry to paper over it.

--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -254,6 +254,24 @@
 		.await
 		.expect("failed to start settings daemon");

+	// Wait for cosmic-settings-daemon to register its D-Bus name before
+	// starting the components below (cosmic-osd, cosmic-panel, etc.) that
+	// watch configs through it. Without this, their first watch_config /
+	// watch_state call can race the daemon's own startup and log a
+	// spurious "Failed to create watcher" error before the daemon-side
+	// retry (with backoff) papers over it a few seconds later.
+	if let Ok(session_conn) = zbus::Connection::session().await
+		&& let Ok(dbus_proxy) = zbus::fdo::DBusProxy::new(&session_conn).await
+		&& let Ok(name) = zbus::names::BusName::from_static_str("com.system76.CosmicSettingsDaemon")
+	{
+		for _ in 0..50 {
+			if matches!(dbus_proxy.name_has_owner(name.clone()).await, Ok(true)) {
+				break;
+			}
+			tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(100)).await;
+		}
+	}
+
 	// notifying the user service manager that we've reached the
 	// graphical-session.target, which should only happen after:
 	// - cosmic-comp is ready
